  "body": "- Deleting a folder now also deletes folder-scoped Variables (browse UI and App Platform cascade).\r\n- Folder empty-checks / counts include Variables.\r\n- Removes the Variable RBAC orphan-cleanup path from #129470.\r\n\r\nDepends on grafana/grafana-enterprise#13284 for MT folders apiserver (injects the Variable client).\r\n\r\n@grafana/grafana-dashboards-core I created this diagram for an architecture overview since we haven't interacted with folder cascade delete before\r\n\r\n<img width=\"2274\" height=\"1658\" alt=\"Cascade-delete folder Variables — architecture - 1  Two delete paths\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c191b7b8-b89a-4cdf-bc59-a58add8fe3ae\" />\r\n\r\nFixes https://github.com/grafana/grafana/issues/130646\r\n\r\n### Test plan\r\n- [x] Delete a folder from browse that contains Variables — Variables are gone\r\n- [x] Nested folder delete removes Variables in child folders",
  "changed_files": 18,
